From: baseband lane
Subject: 0534 pandora_mpss: cross the modem's images with the ADSP's ids, and log the assign addresses

Two questions that one boot can now answer.

1. The cross probe only ever compared {modem_dtb, modem} against {4, 38}, so it could not tell
   whether the refusal is about the ID or about the IMAGE.  It now also sends those images as pas 13
   and pas 36 -- the ids the secure world accepts for the ADSP on this very phone -- and the plan is
   to try the ADSP's own zap as pas 4 in the same spirit.  Either answer ends the guessing:
     * modem blob accepted as 13 -> the id is what is refused;
     * still refused      -> TrustZone is judging the image against the id, so the blob pair is wrong.

2. The assign now prints every address that went into the call (the page's physical address, the
   sources, the destinations, the argument tail).  The 2026-11-23 03:1x boot ran the upstream-shaped
   assign and still got 0xffffffffffffffff, which an SMC64 uses for "call not accepted at all".  The
   one thing the code cannot verify before the call is what pmap_find_phys() returned for the page;
   printing it says whether that is the problem or the descriptor still is.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c b/b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
index 7c58eea..d4d4173 100755
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
@@ -104,6 +104,7 @@ extern void pandora_scm_call(uint64_t fn, uint64_t arginfo, uint64_t x2, uint64_
 #define MP_PAS            4u             /* canoe_mpss_resource, decoded from qcom_q6v5_pas.ko */
 #define MP_PAS_DTB        0x26u          /* 38 */
 #define MP_PAS_CONTROL    13u            /* the ADSP's zap id: known-good for INIT_IMAGE */
+#define MP_PAS_ADSP1      36u            /* the ADSP's second id, also accepted in every boot so far */
 static unsigned mp_pas = MP_PAS, mp_pas_dtb = MP_PAS_DTB;
 #define MP_IPA_FW_PA      0x99580000ull  /* ipa_fw_region@99580000: 0x10000 */
 #define MP_IPA_FW_SIZE    0x10000ull
@@ -349,8 +350,18 @@ mp_assign_region(uint64_t region_pa, uint64_t region_size)
 	__asm__ volatile ("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
 	pandora_scm_call5(PANDORA_SCM_MP_ASSIGN, PANDORA_SCM_ASSIGN_ARGUMENTS, pa, 16, pa + 64,
 	    pa + 240, &a0, &a1);
-	printf("PANDORA MPSS: assign %#llx+%#llx to MSS -> a0 %#llx a1 %#llx %s\n", region_pa,
-	    region_size, a0, a1, (a0 || a1) ? "REFUSED" : "ok");
+	/*
+	 * Print every address that went into the call, not just the answer.
+	 *
+	 * The 2026-11-23 03:1x boot ran the upstream-shaped call and still got
+	 * 0xffffffffffffffff, which for an SMC64 means the secure world did not accept the call at
+	 * all.  With the page's physical address in the log the next run can say whether that is
+	 * because pmap_find_phys() returned something unusable (the one thing the code cannot check
+	 * before the call) or because the descriptor itself is still wrong.
+	 */
+	printf("PANDORA MPSS: assign %#llx+%#llx to MSS (page %#llx src %#llx dest %#llx more %#llx) "
+	    "-> a0 %#llx a1 %#llx %s\n", region_pa, region_size, pa, pa + 64, pa + 128, pa + 240,
+	    a0, a1, (a0 || a1) ? "REFUSED" : "ok");
 	kmem_free(kernel_map, (vm_offset_t)page, PAGE_SIZE);
 	return (a0 == 0 && a1 == 0);
 }
@@ -993,12 +1004,24 @@ static void
 mp_probe_cross(void)
 {
 	static const char *const images[] = { "modem_dtb", "modem" };
-	static const unsigned ids[] = { MP_PAS, MP_PAS_DTB };
+	/*
+	 * Not just the modem's own ids.  Two questions are worth one boot each way:
+	 *
+	 *   - is the refusal about the ID?  Then the modem's blob paired with an id the secure world
+	 *     already accepts for other images (13, 36 -- the ADSP's) should be taken;
+	 *   - or is it about the IMAGE?  Then the ADSP's own zap, which TrustZone accepts as pas 13,
+	 *     should be refused when sent as pas 4.
+	 *
+	 * Whichever way it comes out, the answer stops the guessing: until now every cross was inside
+	 * {4, 38} and so could not separate the two.
+	 */
+	static const unsigned ids[] = { MP_PAS, MP_PAS_DTB, MP_PAS_CONTROL, MP_PAS_ADSP1 };
 
 	if (!mp_option("pandora_mpss_pas_probe2")) {
 		return;
 	}
-	printf("PANDORA MPSS: crossing 2 images with 2 PAS ids, each with its own metadata\n");
+	printf("PANDORA MPSS: crossing 2 images with %u PAS ids (4, 38, 13, 36), each with its own metadata\n",
+	    (unsigned)(sizeof(ids) / sizeof(ids[0])));
 	for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(images) / sizeof(images[0]); i++) {
 		for (unsigned j = 0; j < sizeof(ids) / sizeof(ids[0]); j++) {
 			uint64_t answer = 0;
